.\" Man page for sniptext
.TH SNIPTEXT 1 "2026" "sniptext" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sniptext \- screen-capture OCR with per-image Tesseract preprocessing
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sniptext
[\fB\-h\fR] [\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fB\-c\fR \fICONFIG\fR] [\fB\-v\fR]
[\fB\-\-capture\-now\fR | \fB\-\-file\fR \fIIMAGE\fR]
[\fB\-\-print\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-output\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-\-history\fR [\fIN\fR]] [\fB\-\-profile\fR \fINAME\fR]
[\fB\-\-list\-profiles\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sniptext
lets you select a screen region, recognises its text with Tesseract and
copies the text to the clipboard.  Run without arguments it captures once
and exits.  Bind \fBsniptext \-\-capture\-now\fR to a key in your compositor.
.PP
For each image a small model predicts the character error rate of each
shipped preprocessing pipeline and the program runs the one with the best
predicted accuracy for its time.  If that pipeline returns no text, the
default pipeline runs instead.  Images above 2 megapixels are not routed.
.PP
After a screen capture a desktop notification shows the start of the text,
or the reason when Tesseract could not run.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-version
Print the version string and exit.
.TP
.BR \-c " \fICONFIG\fR, " \-\-config " \fICONFIG\fR"
Path to a YAML configuration file.
Default: \fI~/.config/sniptext/config.yaml\fR.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable debug logging to stderr.
.TP
.B \-\-capture\-now
Select a screen region and recognise it.  This is the default action.
Cannot be combined with \fB\-\-file\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-file " \fIIMAGE\fR"
Run OCR on an existing image file instead of capturing the screen.
Supports any format that Pillow can open.  Transparent areas are treated
as white.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-config
Print the current configuration in YAML format with comments and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-output " \fIFILE\fR"
Write the recognised text to \fIFILE\fR in addition to copying it to the
clipboard.
.TP
.BR \-\-history " [\fIN\fR]"
Print the last \fIN\fR captured texts (default: 10) with their timestamps
and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-profile " \fINAME\fR"
Load \fI~/.config/sniptext/profiles/NAME.yaml\fR and merge its values on
top of the base configuration.  Only the fields to override need to be
present in the profile file.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-profiles
List available profiles and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, or no text was found.
.TP
.B 1
The capture, the OCR or the clipboard failed.
.TP
.B 2
Unreadable image file or bad arguments.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration file is a YAML document located at
\fI~/.config/sniptext/config.yaml\fR by default.  It is created on first
run.  Keys of removed features are ignored with a warning.
.TP
.B ocr_language
Tesseract language code(s).  For multiple languages use \fB+\fR as
separator, e.g. \fIeng+rus\fR.  Default: \fIeng\fR.
.TP
.B routing
Choose the preprocessing pipeline per image.  With \fIfalse\fR the default
pipeline always runs.  Default: \fItrue\fR.
.TP
.B router_time_weight
Error traded per second in that choice.  Blank uses the benchmarked value,
\fI0\fR ignores time.
.TP
.B max_image_size
Images with a larger side are reduced before OCR.  Default: \fI4096\fR.
.TP
.B notification_enabled
Show a desktop notification after each capture.  Default: \fItrue\fR.
.TP
.B history_enabled " / " history_size
Keep captured texts and set how many.  Defaults: \fItrue\fR / \fI50\fR.
.TP
.B display_server
\fIauto\fR, \fIwayland\fR or \fIx11\fR.  Default: \fIauto\fR.
.SS Profiles
Create partial YAML files in \fI~/.config/sniptext/profiles/\fR to define
named presets.
.PP
Example \- \fI~/.config/sniptext/profiles/rus.yaml\fR:
.PP
.nf
    ocr_language: eng+rus
.fi
.PP
Activate with: \fBsniptext \-\-profile rus \-\-capture\-now\fR
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/sniptext/config.yaml
Main configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.config/sniptext/profiles/
Directory for named configuration profiles.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/sniptext/history.jsonl
Capture history (one JSON object per line).
.SH EXAMPLES
Capture a region and copy its text:
.PP
.nf
    sniptext \-\-capture\-now
.fi
.PP
Run OCR on an existing file and save the result:
.PP
.nf
    sniptext \-\-file screenshot.png \-\-output result.txt
.fi
.PP
Show the last 20 captured texts:
.PP
.nf
    sniptext \-\-history 20
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tesseract (1),
.BR notify-send (1),
.BR wl-copy (1),
.BR xclip (1)
